1
00:00:05,030 --> 00:00:05,900
Physics.

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,670
Whoa, finally! It's been way too long.

3
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:10,430
I've picked all my universities.

4
00:00:10,430 --> 00:00:11,500
I kind of cheated on London.

5
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,700
What made you change your mind?

6
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:16,270
It's been so long. You were really cool back there, Din.

7
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:17,700
Can I get a hug?

8
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,230
I hope things go well for you, Yok.

9
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:20,000
Okay.

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,670
Come have moo kratha at my place.

11
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:26,270
I can't peel shrimp.

12
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:27,430
Just say so next time.

13
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:29,230
I'll peel them for you.

14
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,170
Thank you, Din.

15
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:34,430
Why not clean the wound? At least put some ointment on it.

16
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,900
Shift back a little.

17
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:40,260
Welcome, everyone, to the 11th Science Smart Camp,

18
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:41,400
officially.

19
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:44,970
So let's start with... the first activity.

20
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,270
And each group will have...

21
00:00:51,130 --> 00:00:53,570
Everyone, let's all listen to Star.

22
00:00:59,630 --> 00:01:01,830
If it's bothering you, shouldn't you make a decision?

23
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:02,930
I'm scared of losing my friends.

24
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:04,129
I'm the one who likes you.

25
00:01:04,129 --> 00:01:05,600
So it's on me to deal with my own feelings.

26
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,500
The promise you made me when I was a kid,

27
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:09,230
do you still remember it?

28
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,400
Hey, everyone, help! Star fell in the water!

29
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:24,130
The activity he came up with costs too much.

30
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:25,670
And it definitely can't be family money.

31
00:01:25,670 --> 00:01:27,470
I already told you, I'll find a way.

32
00:01:27,470 --> 00:01:28,870
Change the singer. I'm asking you.

33
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:31,700
And I still don't understand why you're picking a fight with me.

34
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:33,300
He's someone who's always ready to cause trouble.

35
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:34,900
Not here to lecture you. I'm here to help.

36
00:01:36,830 --> 00:01:38,070
Everyone, step outside.

37
00:01:38,270 --> 00:01:41,030
Star. Star, are you okay?

38
00:01:42,470 --> 00:01:43,900
Star, can you hear me?

39
00:01:48,870 --> 00:01:50,870
Satayu, sweetheart... Star.

40
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:12,530
Satayu.

41
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,070
Satayu.

42
00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:16,530
Ms. James. / Yes, dear.

43
00:02:17,630 --> 00:02:18,430
Din.

44
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:19,400
How are you feeling?

45
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,370
Are you okay, sweetheart? Can you sit up?

46
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,570
I'm fine. Totally fine.

47
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:47,100
You scared me half to death. You were out cold for a whole night.

48
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,430
I'm sorry. / It's all right, it's all right.

49
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,070
As long as you're okay, as long as you're safe, that's all that matters.

50
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,470
Thank you too, Din.

51
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:02,870
And the camp right now...

52
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:05,830
Don't you worry about the camp.

53
00:03:05,830 --> 00:03:07,300
Take care of yourself first.

54
00:03:09,770 --> 00:03:10,770
You're sure you're okay?

55
00:03:11,670 --> 00:03:12,800
I'm okay.

56
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:16,070
Phoodin, look after him.

57
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:24,100
Star, you're sure?

58
00:03:25,270 --> 00:03:26,270
I'm okay, ma'am.

59
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:29,770
Then if you're really okay,

60
00:03:29,770 --> 00:03:31,730
the camp activities carry on.

61
00:03:32,270 --> 00:03:34,870
But I mean it, look after each other, Phoodin.

62
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:36,770
And don't let an accident like this happen again.

63
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:40,930
Okay, okay.

64
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:43,970
Thank you so much, teacher.

65
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,770
Ow.

66
00:03:47,770 --> 00:03:49,870
What a relief for you all.

67
00:03:57,730 --> 00:03:59,070
Okay.

68
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:00,830
Teu went down too.

69
00:04:00,830 --> 00:04:02,070
Teu got himself a cut.

70
00:04:02,070 --> 00:04:03,670
So how are you?

71
00:04:03,670 --> 00:04:05,600
Okay, but it still hurts a bit.

72
00:04:07,470 --> 00:04:11,430
Shall we get back to the camp? See it through to the end.

73
00:04:11,430 --> 00:04:12,230
Let's do it!

74
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:06,830
The promise you made me when I was a kid,

75
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:09,430
do you still remember it?

76
00:07:30,470 --> 00:07:32,200
So what are you going to do now, huh?

77
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,770
You went and talked to him like that.

78
00:07:33,770 --> 00:07:35,430
He was still stammering.

79
00:07:35,430 --> 00:07:37,130
I don't think so.

80
00:07:40,670 --> 00:07:43,430
I think... maybe I should just stop.

81
00:07:44,530 --> 00:07:45,330
Est.

82
00:07:45,730 --> 00:07:46,770
Let me borrow your phone.

83
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:47,700
What for?

84
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:48,870
Order some dog food.

85
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:50,200
Whoa, that's the one.

86
00:07:50,770 --> 00:07:52,320
I bet we're getting another round, man.

87
00:07:52,330 --> 00:07:54,930
But I think... this time I'm serious.

88
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,530
Ow.

89
00:07:56,530 --> 00:07:58,230
Hey, order some for me too.

90
00:07:58,770 --> 00:07:59,570
Which brand?

91
00:07:59,570 --> 00:08:01,130
Make it two, or I won't be full.

92
00:08:01,130 --> 00:08:02,600
Go for it, man.

93
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,130
Are you even my friend?

94
00:08:12,030 --> 00:08:13,330
For real. / Seriously?

95
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,530
Hey, Aof's here.

96
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,770
Oh no. What do we do now?

97
00:08:26,470 --> 00:08:27,370
Are you going to talk to him?

98
00:08:28,030 --> 00:08:30,130
I... I'm not.

99
00:08:30,430 --> 00:08:31,630
I'm not ready.

100
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,500
I think you should go home.

101
00:08:51,070 --> 00:08:53,830
My friend isn't feeling up to it.

102
00:08:53,830 --> 00:08:57,300
Yeah. Whichever way you came, go back the same way.

103
00:08:57,730 --> 00:08:59,370
You may be my idol,

104
00:09:00,130 --> 00:09:02,170
but I have to protect my friend.

105
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:08,230
I think you should wait and talk tomorrow.

106
00:09:08,230 --> 00:09:10,130
If Chemi wants to talk, you'll get your chance.

107
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:14,230
I can't. This is important.

108
00:09:14,770 --> 00:09:16,870
I don't want Chemi misunderstanding me.

109
00:09:25,070 --> 00:09:26,570
Could you all help me out?

110
00:09:29,470 --> 00:09:30,470
No.

111
00:09:30,970 --> 00:09:33,770
But promise us, if we help you this time,

112
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:36,730
you'll do everything we ask.

113
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,900
Everything, really?

114
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,300
Zac.

115
00:09:43,830 --> 00:09:45,230
Then tell me this.

116
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:48,100
Does saying that mean you already have an answer for my friend?

117
00:09:51,070 --> 00:09:54,630
Right. Isn't it that you have no answer at all,

118
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:56,900
and you just came to test my friend's feelings?

119
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:02,230
Then let us tell you...

120
00:10:02,770 --> 00:10:05,800
how our friend is doing, and what you should do now.

121
00:10:13,930 --> 00:10:15,830
My friend's doing just fine.

122
00:10:15,830 --> 00:10:17,300
You don't need to worry that much.

123
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:19,270
So you can head home now.

124
00:10:20,470 --> 00:10:21,830
It's probably better for you.

125
00:10:24,730 --> 00:10:26,430
I think you should go.

126
00:10:29,270 --> 00:10:30,600
Chemi.

127
00:10:34,170 --> 00:10:36,370
I still want to talk to you, Chemi.

128
00:10:46,530 --> 00:10:48,230
Please just go home.

129
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:09,770
Chemi, Aof's gone.

130
00:11:30,270 --> 00:11:31,900
I get you now.

131
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:18,100
Then I'll hand it over to the M.4 juniors.

132
00:14:36,130 --> 00:14:38,830
Thank you. Thank you.

133
00:15:17,770 --> 00:15:18,570
What's bugging you?

134
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:22,970
Nothing.

135
00:15:27,030 --> 00:15:29,130
You can talk to me about anything.

136
00:15:29,130 --> 00:15:30,770
I won't tell anyone.

137
00:15:31,170 --> 00:15:32,270
I promise.

138
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:38,530
It's nothing really.

139
00:15:39,230 --> 00:15:41,400
I just haven't been feeling good about it.

140
00:15:44,430 --> 00:15:46,400
When Star fell in the water,

141
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,130
all I could do was shout.

142
00:15:48,130 --> 00:15:50,470
I couldn't actually help him at all.

143
00:15:54,070 --> 00:15:56,900
But I think it was your shouting, Time,

144
00:15:59,700 --> 00:16:01,970
that let everyone know Star had fallen in.

145
00:16:11,730 --> 00:16:12,830
I'm hungry.

146
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,000
Want to grab a bite together?

147
00:16:16,470 --> 00:16:18,570
No thanks. You go ahead.

148
00:17:00,030 --> 00:17:01,570
Think it over again.

149
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,430
No thanks. You go ahead.

150
00:17:12,130 --> 00:17:14,400
But I'm worried it's too spicy.

151
00:17:14,970 --> 00:17:16,630
Time, can you taste it for me?

152
00:17:17,470 --> 00:17:20,099
If you're worried it's spicy, why not use half a packet?

153
00:17:20,430 --> 00:17:24,230
Come on, the makers already figured it out — this much is what tastes right.

154
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,170
Just do it.

155
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:27,700
Taste it for me, please.

156
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,370
Not spicy. It's good.

157
00:18:00,930 --> 00:18:01,930
Really?

158
00:18:02,670 --> 00:18:04,900
But I think I took too few noodles just now.

159
00:18:05,170 --> 00:18:06,570
One more time?

160
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:14,500
Then I'll have some.

161
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:27,600
Not spicy at all. It's good.

162
00:18:29,270 --> 00:18:31,200
But if you're going to eat this much,

163
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,430
why not just eat with me?

164
00:18:34,830 --> 00:18:37,670
Your stomach's that loud, why hold back?

165
00:18:38,730 --> 00:18:40,400
You heard that?

166
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,570
Loud and clear.

167
00:18:44,100 --> 00:18:46,700
It's just, lately I feel so guilty.

168
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:48,800
I study late, right?

169
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:50,330
So I got into late-night eating.

170
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:52,700
Before I knew it, my pants got tight.

171
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:55,270
So I decided to quit eating late.

172
00:18:57,930 --> 00:19:00,300
It's fine. We'll start over tomorrow.

173
00:19:00,770 --> 00:19:02,570
If you're hungry today, you eat.

174
00:19:02,970 --> 00:19:05,030
I'm not making you eat alone, Time.

175
00:19:07,430 --> 00:19:10,670
I'll eat with you, so you don't have to feel guilty.

176
00:19:17,070 --> 00:19:18,830
You really are something.

177
00:19:19,630 --> 00:19:21,270
Fine, let's eat. Come on.

178
00:19:21,270 --> 00:19:22,770
Here, go ahead.

179
00:19:23,430 --> 00:19:24,800
Put it right here.

180
00:19:28,100 --> 00:19:29,930
I'll dig in.

181
00:19:40,130 --> 00:19:41,830
I'll dig in, then.

182
00:19:46,930 --> 00:19:48,200
Refreshing.

183
00:19:48,570 --> 00:19:49,770
Want a meatball?

184
00:19:50,170 --> 00:19:50,970
Here.

185
00:19:55,330 --> 00:19:57,900
Nice and big.

186
00:20:17,030 --> 00:20:18,130
Physics.

187
00:20:21,170 --> 00:20:23,130
So you're not going after him?

188
00:20:23,130 --> 00:20:24,530
If you think I'm him...

189
00:20:26,170 --> 00:20:28,330
He said he was just going to get water.

190
00:20:29,630 --> 00:20:30,930
By now the whole pond's probably gone.

191
00:20:31,670 --> 00:20:33,570
I saw him sitting over there like some music-video heartthrob.

192
00:20:33,570 --> 00:20:36,400
So why didn't you bring him back to the tent?

193
00:20:36,970 --> 00:20:39,830
You think if I went after him, he'd just come back with me?

194
00:20:40,330 --> 00:20:44,070
You think I'd walk in there and play the music-video heartthrob opposite him, like—

195
00:20:45,230 --> 00:20:47,730
Mr. Physics, I'm Fuen.

196
00:20:48,770 --> 00:20:51,030
Mr. Physics, would you come back to the tent with me?

197
00:20:51,030 --> 00:20:52,030
Please?

198
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:05,830
Honestly, I just don't want to get involved with you two anymore.

199
00:21:06,230 --> 00:21:08,100
I can barely handle my own life.

200
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:14,830
About Chemi, just talk to Physics straight.

201
00:21:15,800 --> 00:21:18,330
You're always so good at this when it's my problem.

202
00:21:18,330 --> 00:21:20,900
How about this: you and I go at the same time,

203
00:21:23,230 --> 00:21:25,070
and sit down and talk separately.

204
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:31,800
I'm staying out of it.

205
00:21:35,170 --> 00:21:37,870
I mean... I don't even know what I'm supposed to do.

206
00:21:37,870 --> 00:21:40,470
By now I know that... I like him.

207
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:45,900
But when he came and said to me,

208
00:21:47,300 --> 00:21:48,900
Do you still remember that day?

209
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:50,430
it made me feel like...

210
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:53,970
I don't know if he really likes me, or if he's just...

211
00:21:57,930 --> 00:21:59,730
hung up on what was said.

212
00:22:02,170 --> 00:22:05,130
Have you ever just asked him straight?

213
00:22:05,470 --> 00:22:07,300
And have you ever done that with Physics?

214
00:22:07,300 --> 00:22:09,170
Just come out and ask him.

215
00:22:15,570 --> 00:22:16,970
It's not the same.

216
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:18,930
How is it not the same?

217
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:22,600
Physics has made it so damn obvious he's liked you since M.2.

218
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:30,530
I'm Physics. I just transferred here. Nice to meet you.

219
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:00,800
M.2?

220
00:23:01,270 --> 00:23:03,730
Yeah, you idiot.

221
00:23:03,730 --> 00:23:05,000
You really had no idea?

222
00:23:07,030 --> 00:23:09,400
Since M.2. Think about it.

223
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:11,800
He kept you and me apart like a monk and a woman — no touching allowed.

224
00:23:12,370 --> 00:23:14,670
Tang and I could barely even touch you.

225
00:23:22,530 --> 00:23:24,430
Does the power never go out at your place?

226
00:23:24,430 --> 00:23:25,900
Light a candle once in a while, Fuen.

227
00:23:32,130 --> 00:23:33,430
It's from me.

228
00:23:41,830 --> 00:23:43,470
Why'd you buy me candles?

229
00:23:45,730 --> 00:23:46,870
In case your power goes out.

230
00:23:47,830 --> 00:23:49,200
Light them right away.

231
00:23:53,530 --> 00:23:55,900
How much longer are you going to leave me standing in the sun?

232
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:58,670
It's hot. Let's go to school. It's getting hot.

233
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:01,870
Hurry.

234
00:24:57,700 --> 00:24:59,170
I'll be back, then.

235
00:25:35,770 --> 00:25:38,930
You'd sleep right here if I hadn't come, wouldn't you?

236
00:26:06,830 --> 00:26:08,430
If I hadn't come,

237
00:26:09,930 --> 00:26:11,930
you weren't going back to your room?

238
00:26:13,930 --> 00:26:14,730
Of course I was.

239
00:26:16,930 --> 00:26:18,730
I just wanted to give you space.

240
00:26:20,070 --> 00:26:21,600
After I told you that,

241
00:26:23,600 --> 00:26:25,730
you've been thinking about it all day, haven't you?

242
00:26:33,630 --> 00:26:35,300
I just found out from Aof

243
00:26:37,300 --> 00:26:38,000
that...

244
00:26:38,670 --> 00:26:40,400
you've liked me since M.2?

245
00:27:28,030 --> 00:27:29,670
How did you stand it?

246
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:52,430
Because I like you so damn much.

247
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:02,270
I don't know...

248
00:28:04,670 --> 00:28:07,230
what you're like when you like someone.

249
00:28:14,070 --> 00:28:15,370
But for me,

250
00:28:28,900 --> 00:28:31,200
I never saw you as just a friend to begin with.

251
00:28:40,970 --> 00:28:43,730
I'm scared, Physics.

252
00:28:53,530 --> 00:28:56,300
I'm scared that if I cross that line,

253
00:28:58,230 --> 00:29:00,700
and I lose the best friend I have in you,

254
00:29:03,430 --> 00:29:05,170
I couldn't take it.

255
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:32,730
I understand.

256
00:29:36,500 --> 00:29:38,370
It's okay. I can wait.

257
00:29:44,930 --> 00:29:51,900
No. This time you're the one who draws the line for us.

258
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:05,470
Then at the school event this year,

259
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:10,330
watch the fireworks with me.

260
00:31:00,730 --> 00:31:02,270
Not going back to sleep?

261
00:31:03,170 --> 00:31:04,800
I can't sleep.

262
00:31:07,400 --> 00:31:08,770
Want to sleep together, then?

263
00:31:09,930 --> 00:31:11,430
You already sleep at my place, don't you?

264
00:32:12,430 --> 00:32:14,000
You okay?

265
00:32:17,900 --> 00:32:20,930
And are you okay, Din?

266
00:32:28,130 --> 00:32:29,370
Okay.

267
00:32:30,070 --> 00:32:32,030
I talked to Fuen.

268
00:32:36,030 --> 00:32:38,130
At least I didn't lose a friend.

269
00:32:42,230 --> 00:32:45,170
But taking the person my friend likes,

270
00:32:47,870 --> 00:32:49,870
I just can't do it.

271
00:32:50,530 --> 00:32:51,670
Exactly.

272
00:32:52,900 --> 00:32:57,130
I'm... not good at taking someone out of another person's heart either.

273
00:33:00,570 --> 00:33:03,500
Letting go yourself is much easier, Din.

274
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:07,270
And besides, my dad taught me that

275
00:33:07,630 --> 00:33:10,130
he raised me with love

276
00:33:12,170 --> 00:33:13,800
and happiness.

277
00:33:14,400 --> 00:33:18,670
So I must never let anyone make me sad.

278
00:33:27,930 --> 00:33:29,800
Oh, Din.

279
00:33:32,700 --> 00:33:35,870
I'd like to get your contact.

280
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:42,800
I want to pay you back for saving me when I fell in the water.

281
00:33:43,470 --> 00:33:45,570
No need. It was just my job.

282
00:33:45,570 --> 00:33:49,470
Job or not, I feel like I have to...

283
00:33:50,270 --> 00:33:52,070
give you something back.

284
00:33:54,800 --> 00:33:57,030
At least let me take you out for a meal, Din.

285
00:33:58,930 --> 00:34:01,330
Why do you like taking people out to eat so much?

286
00:34:06,870 --> 00:34:09,670
Then whenever I'm hungry,

287
00:34:10,429 --> 00:34:12,130
I'll just get Star's contact from someone else.

288
00:34:12,600 --> 00:34:14,699
Why would you get it from someone else?

289
00:34:14,699 --> 00:34:16,929
Why not just ask me right now?

290
00:34:17,969 --> 00:34:20,730
If you got it from someone else, or my friends found out,

291
00:34:21,929 --> 00:34:24,429
my contact doesn't come that easy, Din.

292
00:34:25,070 --> 00:34:25,870
Hey.

293
00:34:25,870 --> 00:34:27,800
Mine doesn't come easy either.

294
00:34:28,130 --> 00:34:30,170
People at school sell mine.

295
00:34:30,170 --> 00:34:31,230
For good money.

296
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:35,170
But mine is very expensive, Din.

297
00:34:35,929 --> 00:34:37,830
I think I can afford it.

298
00:34:37,830 --> 00:34:40,600
Then it's up to you.

299
00:34:42,230 --> 00:34:44,600
Consider yourself warned.

300
00:35:04,230 --> 00:35:07,130
Est, Jay, and Chemi.

301
00:35:08,730 --> 00:35:10,270
Go ahead, go ahead.

302
00:35:13,200 --> 00:35:15,230
Hey, there they are.

303
00:35:15,570 --> 00:35:18,430
That's all of M.5, then.

304
00:35:18,900 --> 00:35:20,500
See you, guys.

305
00:35:20,500 --> 00:35:22,100
See you up there.

306
00:35:23,470 --> 00:35:25,870
The rest of them... check them in.

307
00:35:26,930 --> 00:35:28,470
Check them all.

308
00:35:28,470 --> 00:35:29,970
Is anyone hiding around here?

309
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:31,830
No one's hiding at this point.

310
00:35:31,830 --> 00:35:33,000
They all want to go home.

311
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:35,700
Just Aof left...

312
00:35:40,500 --> 00:35:42,300
All of M.6 is here.

313
00:35:45,900 --> 00:35:47,300
Okay. / All present.

314
00:35:47,300 --> 00:35:48,370
Right. / All present, then.

315
00:36:16,870 --> 00:36:18,800
I know you're not asleep.

316
00:36:20,900 --> 00:36:22,630
Are you really going to let him go?

317
00:36:26,100 --> 00:36:29,570
I don't know what to do next.

318
00:36:30,400 --> 00:36:34,170
My question wasn't as hard as you made it out to be, was it?

319
00:36:36,530 --> 00:36:38,930
I've tried to understand him, but

320
00:36:40,070 --> 00:36:41,800
I still don't get him.

321
00:36:44,070 --> 00:36:46,370
Then keep your distance for a while.

322
00:36:47,100 --> 00:36:48,630
Stick with us.

323
00:36:51,200 --> 00:36:52,700
Don't you guys leave me.

324
00:36:54,070 --> 00:36:57,600
Even if I'm being an idiot, don't you dare leave me.

325
00:36:58,570 --> 00:37:00,770
Yeah, no one's leaving you.

326
00:37:00,770 --> 00:37:02,870
If we did, no one else would take you.

327
00:37:03,530 --> 00:37:06,170
But I want to be with you. All of you.

328
00:37:06,170 --> 00:37:07,170
Oh.

329
00:37:08,670 --> 00:37:11,070
You could just leave me and Zac alone together.

330
00:37:11,730 --> 00:37:14,200
And leave me with Est? No thanks.

331
00:37:16,300 --> 00:37:20,630
Then let's keep being this gloriously pointless little squad.

332
00:37:20,630 --> 00:37:21,970
Sounds good, man.

333
00:37:43,100 --> 00:37:46,230
Hey, now that camp's over,

334
00:37:46,230 --> 00:37:51,000
I think we should start talking about Thapfah Countdown.

335
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:55,500
No problem. I've already got some of the details ready.

336
00:37:55,500 --> 00:37:58,900
By the way, do you want it open to outsiders or students only?

337
00:37:59,430 --> 00:38:01,030
Open to outsiders, like every year.

338
00:38:01,030 --> 00:38:03,030
Ticket price stays the same.

339
00:38:03,030 --> 00:38:04,630
As for the performances,

340
00:38:04,630 --> 00:38:06,670
I think each class should pitch

341
00:38:06,670 --> 00:38:08,070
what they want to do,

342
00:38:08,600 --> 00:38:10,030
and we'll see where we can support them.

343
00:38:10,030 --> 00:38:12,200
I'll handle the booths myself.

344
00:38:12,630 --> 00:38:14,500
I think we can use last year's vendor.

345
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:16,630
All good. We'll talk later.

346
00:38:17,100 --> 00:38:19,800
We've still got a month or so before the event.

347
00:38:26,600 --> 00:38:27,870
Let's go!

348
00:38:41,070 --> 00:38:41,870
Really, Dad?

349
00:38:42,970 --> 00:38:44,670
Oh, Dad, Dad, hold on.

350
00:38:44,670 --> 00:38:46,730
I think our son's back, Dad.

351
00:38:48,970 --> 00:38:51,730
Why didn't you tell us you were coming? I'd have come to get you.

352
00:38:51,730 --> 00:38:52,730
It's fine, Mom.

353
00:38:52,730 --> 00:38:54,230
Getting a ride on the app is easier.

354
00:38:54,230 --> 00:38:55,770
You'd just get stuck in traffic.

355
00:38:55,770 --> 00:38:56,870
So, did you have fun?

356
00:38:57,530 --> 00:38:59,000
Don't tell it yet, don't tell it.

357
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,330
Your dad's right here. Come on.

358
00:39:00,330 --> 00:39:01,500
Dad's calling?

359
00:39:02,230 --> 00:39:03,500
Darling, our son's home.

360
00:39:03,500 --> 00:39:05,030
Hi, Dad.

361
00:39:05,030 --> 00:39:08,300
It was great, and the seniors took really good care of me.

362
00:39:08,300 --> 00:39:11,570
My brother came along too, but he stuck with Fuen as usual.

363
00:39:12,130 --> 00:39:12,930
Really?

364
00:39:12,930 --> 00:39:16,630
So, have you won Fuen over yet?

365
00:39:19,600 --> 00:39:23,200
Not yet, but I'm making progress.

366
00:39:23,200 --> 00:39:25,100
I already told Fuen how I feel.

367
00:39:26,030 --> 00:39:27,270
Really, son?

368
00:39:27,900 --> 00:39:28,770
Yes. / And?

369
00:39:28,770 --> 00:39:30,600
Should I start saving for the dowry?

370
00:39:32,700 --> 00:39:34,930
Whoa, amazing, bro.

371
00:39:34,930 --> 00:39:37,270
Hey, what happened, what happened?

372
00:39:37,270 --> 00:39:40,700
Then I'll clear my schedule and book tickets back to Thailand.

373
00:39:40,700 --> 00:39:43,300
Slow down, Dad.

374
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:48,230
I told Fuen, but he still needs time to think.

375
00:39:50,100 --> 00:39:53,900
But he didn't seem like he'd turn you down, did he?

376
00:39:56,470 --> 00:39:59,900
I'm not bracing myself anymore. I'm all in.

377
00:40:00,600 --> 00:40:03,130
I don't know about that yet, Dad, Mom.

378
00:40:05,170 --> 00:40:07,230
I guess time will tell.

379
00:40:10,800 --> 00:40:12,930
If two people are really meant for each other,

380
00:40:12,930 --> 00:40:15,470
they'll always find their way back to each other.

381
00:40:19,270 --> 00:40:22,200
And how do you know you're meant for each other?

382
00:40:23,130 --> 00:40:24,630
If having you in his life

383
00:40:25,230 --> 00:40:29,600
makes him safer, better off and happier,

384
00:40:30,730 --> 00:40:33,200
then he'll never let you go.

385
00:40:39,570 --> 00:40:40,900
In that case...

386
00:40:42,400 --> 00:40:44,200
I'm pretty confident that...

387
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:47,770
I am a good thing in Fuen's life.

388
00:40:48,570 --> 00:40:51,500
Whoa, bro, a little overconfident?

389
00:40:52,070 --> 00:40:53,500
Hey. / Yes?

390
00:40:55,330 --> 00:41:00,800
Honestly, no, because I think Fuen

391
00:41:00,800 --> 00:41:04,330
definitely won't find a better friend than me.

392
00:41:07,670 --> 00:41:10,070
That's the confidence, son.

393
00:41:10,770 --> 00:41:12,430
But let me tell you, I've seen plenty of these.

394
00:41:12,430 --> 00:41:14,370
The ones who plan too much

395
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:16,400
are the ones who end up not making it.

396
00:41:17,470 --> 00:41:19,170
Mom. Mom.

397
00:41:19,600 --> 00:41:22,470
Let's just say I

398
00:41:22,470 --> 00:41:23,570
definitely won't slip up.

399
00:41:24,330 --> 00:41:26,600
And none of you need to worry about me.

400
00:41:27,030 --> 00:41:29,600
What you should worry about

401
00:41:29,600 --> 00:41:33,670
is your youngest son right here.

402
00:41:33,670 --> 00:41:37,670
His life's been quite the mess lately.

403
00:41:38,600 --> 00:41:42,630
What is it, son? What's going on? Why didn't you tell me?

404
00:41:42,630 --> 00:41:44,100
Oh, come on, bro.

405
00:41:44,370 --> 00:41:45,730
Doing this to your little brother.

406
00:41:45,730 --> 00:41:47,030
Hey. / Yes?

407
00:41:48,230 --> 00:41:50,030
Are you telling them or not?

408
00:41:51,370 --> 00:41:52,600
If you don't, I will.

409
00:41:52,600 --> 00:41:53,870
Fine, I'll tell them.

410
00:41:56,900 --> 00:42:00,730
But could you go somewhere else? Go up to your room. I'll tell them myself.

411
00:42:00,730 --> 00:42:05,130
No, I happen to want the details.

412
00:42:06,900 --> 00:42:07,700
Out with it.

413
00:42:09,830 --> 00:42:10,630
Okay.

414
00:42:25,700 --> 00:42:30,370
♪ When you turn to me, I can't hold your gaze for long ♪

415
00:42:30,370 --> 00:42:36,070
♪ I carry it into my dreams each night, but I can't do a thing about it ♪

416
00:42:36,070 --> 00:42:41,370
♪ Every look you send my way makes my heart shake even more ♪

417
00:42:41,370 --> 00:42:46,370
♪ One slip and I'm imagining things ♪

418
00:42:46,370 --> 00:42:52,200
♪ I slip and give you my heart, I slip and watch you every day ♪

419
00:42:52,200 --> 00:42:56,870
♪ My heart can't take it ♪

420
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:10,370
♪ Beside you every day, but I have to act like I don't care ♪

421
00:43:10,370 --> 00:43:15,970
♪ We stay just friends, so I keep it inside ♪

422
00:43:15,970 --> 00:43:21,530
♪ I want you to know, but I can't cross that line ♪

423
00:43:21,530 --> 00:43:26,200
♪ I know what's between us should stay unsaid ♪

424
00:43:38,570 --> 00:43:43,470
♪ Afraid that if I say it, you'll never look at me the same ♪

425
00:43:43,470 --> 00:43:49,170
♪ Afraid that one day what we have will break ♪

426
00:43:49,170 --> 00:43:54,800
♪ Should I say it, or just let it stay a dream ♪

427
00:43:54,800 --> 00:43:59,470
♪ One slip and I'm imagining things ♪

428
00:43:59,470 --> 00:44:05,300
♪ I slip and give you my heart, I slip and watch you every day ♪

429
00:44:05,300 --> 00:44:08,000
♪ My heart can't take it ♪

430
00:44:08,530 --> 00:44:12,470
"Sleep well. See you tomorrow."

431
00:44:12,470 --> 00:44:14,730
"Sleep well."

432
00:44:15,770 --> 00:44:21,130
♪ Beside you every day, but I have to act like I don't care ♪

433
00:44:21,130 --> 00:44:26,730
♪ We stay just friends, so I keep it inside ♪

434
00:44:26,730 --> 00:44:32,300
♪ I want you to know, but I can't cross that line ♪

435
00:44:32,300 --> 00:44:36,970
♪ I know what's between us should stay unsaid ♪

436
00:44:44,100 --> 00:44:46,400
"Star, do you have some time tomorrow?"

437
00:44:46,400 --> 00:44:48,400
"There's something I want to talk about."

438
00:45:05,400 --> 00:45:07,930
I'm sorry, Star.

439
00:45:09,170 --> 00:45:11,770
I really can't help you anymore, Star.

440
00:45:13,330 --> 00:45:15,870
It's okay. I understand.

441
00:45:17,130 --> 00:45:20,330
And you don't need to think about me anymore, Fuen.

442
00:45:23,130 --> 00:45:25,970
I'm really okay now.

443
00:45:25,970 --> 00:45:28,500
Okay. Really, Star?

444
00:45:28,500 --> 00:45:29,900
Really.

445
00:45:32,300 --> 00:45:35,030
There's one more thing I want to ask you, Star.

446
00:45:36,170 --> 00:45:37,600
What is it?

447
00:45:38,770 --> 00:45:39,930
That camera.

448
00:45:41,700 --> 00:45:44,270
Can I buy it from you?

449
00:45:49,100 --> 00:45:50,200
Sure.

450
00:45:50,200 --> 00:45:53,030
Let's call it the end of our deal.

451
00:45:55,100 --> 00:45:55,900
Thanks.

452
00:45:56,200 --> 00:45:57,200
But...

453
00:45:57,430 --> 00:46:00,670
now that we're like brothers, it's full price.

454
00:46:00,670 --> 00:46:02,830
No discount.

455
00:46:02,830 --> 00:46:04,200
Star.

456
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:07,430
Your family's rich already.

457
00:46:07,430 --> 00:46:10,230
Can't you give me a discount? Come on.

458
00:46:10,230 --> 00:46:11,500
Do you want it or not?

459
00:46:11,500 --> 00:46:12,630
I'll take it.

460
00:46:13,770 --> 00:46:15,800
I'll transfer the money.

461
00:46:15,800 --> 00:46:17,300
Same account.

462
00:46:17,300 --> 00:46:18,230
Yes, dear.

463
00:46:30,730 --> 00:46:32,370
Transfer late and I'm keeping it.

464
00:46:32,370 --> 00:46:34,170
Transferring now.

465
00:46:42,930 --> 00:46:45,330
I think the stage play this year looks really interesting.

466
00:46:45,330 --> 00:46:48,500
And with a good script to work with, it'd be even more fun.

467
00:46:50,270 --> 00:46:51,700
I agree.

468
00:46:51,700 --> 00:46:55,170
I heard our school has a famous novelist, right?

469
00:46:55,170 --> 00:46:57,300
Who? I've never heard of them.

470
00:46:57,730 --> 00:47:01,770
If I remember right, his name's Kim, M.5.

471
00:47:01,770 --> 00:47:04,670
But he doesn't show his face on social media.

472
00:47:04,670 --> 00:47:06,970
Super mysterious.

473
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:12,030
I don't know who he is either. We'd have to go find out.

474
00:47:13,130 --> 00:47:14,230
I'll leave that to you, then.

475
00:47:15,070 --> 00:47:17,430
This year's theme is carnival, right?

476
00:47:19,030 --> 00:47:21,330
Since this is our last year,

477
00:47:22,100 --> 00:47:24,200
let's go all out.

478
00:47:24,830 --> 00:47:28,200
Then tell everyone: no limits on ideas this year.

479
00:47:28,200 --> 00:47:30,330
Just make it creative and fun.

480
00:47:30,700 --> 00:47:31,730
Let's do it.

481
00:47:32,430 --> 00:47:33,930
Oh, Din.

482
00:47:33,930 --> 00:47:35,430
Have you talked to Star yet?

483
00:47:35,830 --> 00:47:38,230
About having him do PR with Tonnam.

484
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:41,100
Oh, I totally forgot. Thanks for the reminder.

485
00:47:41,100 --> 00:47:43,600
So why don't you just call him?

486
00:47:44,130 --> 00:47:45,430
I don't have his contact.

487
00:47:45,430 --> 00:47:47,070
And why not?

488
00:47:48,900 --> 00:47:50,070
I never asked.

489
00:47:50,070 --> 00:47:51,770
And why didn't you ask?

490
00:47:53,370 --> 00:47:55,300
Why are you two talking in unison?

491
00:47:55,300 --> 00:47:57,230
All right, all right, I'll go now.

492
00:47:59,300 --> 00:48:00,700
Oh, Din.

493
00:48:04,800 --> 00:48:05,700
No contact.

494
00:48:56,930 --> 00:48:59,370
Say whatever it is.

495
00:49:10,630 --> 00:49:13,530
I know this is the camera you wanted,

496
00:49:15,130 --> 00:49:18,130
and you can't buy it anywhere anymore.

497
00:49:26,570 --> 00:49:29,370
So I bought it off Star.

498
00:49:29,370 --> 00:49:32,630
Which means this camera is mine now.

499
00:49:47,900 --> 00:49:50,370
I bought it for you on purpose.

500
00:49:53,830 --> 00:49:57,000
Please take it.

501
00:50:02,070 --> 00:50:04,200
I'm sorry.

502
00:50:37,970 --> 00:50:40,270
Anything you buy for me on purpose,

503
00:50:42,670 --> 00:50:44,630
I want all of it.

504
00:52:10,400 --> 00:52:13,430
You're really not mad at me anymore?

505
00:52:20,600 --> 00:52:22,330
In the end, if you understand me,

506
00:52:22,330 --> 00:52:24,030
I'm not mad at you.

507
00:52:28,470 --> 00:52:31,330
Your heart is pounding right now.

508
00:52:31,330 --> 00:52:32,530
I like it.

509
00:52:36,730 --> 00:52:39,600
You said you'd give me space and time.

510
00:52:40,570 --> 00:52:45,800
I am. Why... not enough?

511
00:52:47,370 --> 00:52:50,300
Oh, really? That's all I get?

512
00:53:43,230 --> 00:53:49,400
The first photo on this camera, let it be you and me.

513
00:53:53,470 --> 00:53:56,770
You already took it. Why ask?

514
00:54:32,500 --> 00:54:35,130
I waited so long for you, my baby.

515
00:54:36,330 --> 00:54:38,800
So long for someone to bring you to me.

516
00:54:41,100 --> 00:54:43,230
I brought him, didn't I?

517
00:54:46,070 --> 00:54:47,600
Sorry it took a while.

518
00:55:11,770 --> 00:55:15,700
Everyone, turn to page 38.

519
00:55:29,100 --> 00:55:30,600
Excuse me, teacher. / Oh, Din.

520
00:55:30,870 --> 00:55:33,030
Does the student council need to talk to the juniors today?

521
00:55:33,030 --> 00:55:34,170
It's something important.

522
00:55:34,170 --> 00:55:36,300
So could I borrow a moment of your time?

523
00:55:36,300 --> 00:55:37,600
Sure, sure, go ahead.

524
00:55:51,000 --> 00:55:52,570
Hey, juniors.

525
00:55:57,830 --> 00:56:00,030
Could I get Star's contact?

526
00:56:02,870 --> 00:56:04,130
No.

527
00:56:12,530 --> 00:56:14,730
"I usually sell my LINE to girls for 500 each. (Din)"

528
00:56:14,730 --> 00:56:16,500
"Huh. Mine goes for 1,000. (Star)"

529
00:56:17,100 --> 00:56:21,600
"I'm waiting for the day you're my boyfriend."

530
00:56:22,070 --> 00:56:24,100
"So how much longer are you going to play hard to get? (Jay)"

531
00:56:24,100 --> 00:56:26,130
"Trust me, Aof's going to figure out he still likes him. Just look at his eyes. (Zac)"

532
00:56:26,800 --> 00:56:28,870
Today I have an announcement for everyone

533
00:56:28,870 --> 00:56:30,830
about our school event this year.

534
00:56:30,830 --> 00:56:33,470
The event everyone's been waiting for: Thapfah Countdown.

535
00:56:33,470 --> 00:56:36,230
Don't forget to invite that special someone, or the one you've got your eye on,

536
00:56:36,230 --> 00:56:37,600
well in advance.

537
00:56:37,600 --> 00:56:38,730
Mission's here, right?

538
00:56:38,730 --> 00:56:39,530
Easier than you'd think.

539
